        \"relation\": \"EXACT_GENERATOR_FAMILY_EQUIVALENCE to SUN on positive scalar carrier\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"system\": \"Zhu equal division\",\n          \"objects\": [\n            \"q=2^(1/12)\"\n          ],\n          \"relation\": \"ROOT_EXTENSION / SAME OPERATION FORM, NOT SAME SUBGROUP\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"system\": \"Messiaen augmentation/diminution\",\n          \"objects\": [\n            \"duration scaling c and c^-1\"\n          ],\n          \"relation\": \"SAME OPERATION FORM, DIFFERENT CARRIER/SEMANTICS\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"proved_relations\": [\n        \"<R,L> = {2^a 3^b} \\u2245 Z^2\",\n        \"sanfen D=R and U=L^-1\",\n        \"q not in <R,L> but q^12=2\",\n        \"O=RL is constructible\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"FROZEN_EQUIVALENCE_CLASS\"\n    },\n    {\n      ","quote_sha256":"39248b8dba24ed608140d7ef2595c9d64b968b62fd0ad6d979ddf743db51fcff"}]},{"id":"32709e8763ac228cadc7cf5ef11c73eca6ada4257030855cc343ed4279474097","path":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/SUN_DEEP_RECOVERY/SUN_Chinese_Lu_Depth_Pilot_2026-09-28.md","sha256":"66e5d2d763e55411993bfcf4ad07ca4cc0a708f624264e226abf51b90531e9dd","source_status":"source-bounded ideal pipe model; native order and physical idealization explicit","quotes":[{"char_start":5402,"char_end":6476,"line_start":49,"line_end":54,"quote":"Let an ideal reference pipe have length `L₀`. CN-C03's first operation gives `L₁ = (2/3)L₀`. Its second operation gives `L₂ = (4/3)L₁ = (8/9)L₀`. Under the *idealized* inverse length–frequency relation, their frequency ratios against the reference are `3/2` and `9/8`. The second value follows from the **ordered path**; endpoint equality alone would not preserve the sequence or the pipe identities. This is a DERIVED computation from CN-C03, not a new historical source claim.\n\nFive tone positions and twelve lü form two address axes in CN-S03's formalization. Their product yields 60 ordered set-position contexts in that model. It does **not** establish 60 historical pipes, 60 empirically attested modes, or a universal Chinese count. The `T` and `t` actions have different preserved coordinates; an implementation must retain both.\n\nThe twelve-pipe generation, five-position function, and eight-material classification are separate structures. A single unlabeled “Chinese music number” node would erase their relation types and falsely imply a shared generation law.\n\n","quote_sha256":"b017516c8905ac8b011f15b7a380e703c0db837cfcb4907c45def37ac8d2a028"}]},{"id":"7d5a026c9df7d3fdf06382c966729a7cf3da22dbc4a1276c9f809f7a139ce965","path":"data/raw/reconstruction-recovered/73b3171aa010c78121f2d7798011ce36f6e4891f4ef1409d25ed98aaca16fcfc/ChatGPT-Comparative Research Protocol-20261030-1502.md","sha256":"73b3171aa010c78121f2d7798011ce36f6e4891f4ef1409d25ed98aaca16fcfc","source_status":"assistant acknowledgment of already established research, subsequent to direct user correction","quotes":[{"char_start":703384,"char_end":703885,"line_start":13742,"line_end":13743,"quote":"**1\\. The Chinese-Western musical bridge was already established.** The reciprocal $2/3$, $4/3$, and $3/4$ relationships, Chinese pitch generation, the Western harmonic realization, and the Fludd-Kepler monochord bridge belong to the existing SUN foundation. They are not new validation results. The full bridge also includes the $81/80$ comma relationship and the $16/15$ boundary excursion. I should have used those together rather than repeatedly presenting the first three ratios as discoveries.\n\n","quote_sha256":"b382df7ac853238ee79e42f01ce1a55a4683eeca60e781d88496ac62c6cbd50c"}]},{"id":"dd5004b2224cfaa99969f817c12d758ea41d503d4c93e8c680f681b001db7a77","path":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/RELATED_LINEAGES/SUN_AUTHORITATIVE_MUTATION_CHRONOLOGY_2026-10-01.txt","sha256":"def5acfb2239f58fe91efbdab0096feba38a6d3e0a18a9ca20bf1e0e950dff94","source_status":"recovered equation/bridge chronology; source-specific lifted FK formalism","quotes":[{"char_start":13417,"char_end":14032,"line_start":822,"line_end":889,"quote":"Composition is\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n(a,m)\\star(b,n)\r\n=\r\n(ab,m+n)\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nwith physical realization\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\Phi(a,m)=a\\,2^{-m}.\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nFor the FK loop\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\gamma_{\\rm FK}\r\n=\r\ne_{\\rm out}e_{\\rm return},\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nwe obtain\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n(r,\\delta)(\\gamma_{\\rm FK})\r\n=\r\n\\left(\r\n\\frac{16}{15},0\r\n\\right)\r\n\\star\r\n\\left(\r\n\\frac{15}{16},1\r\n\\right)\r\n=\r\n(1,1).\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nTherefore\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\Phi(1,1)=\\frac12.\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nThe local harmonic ratios close:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\frac{16}{15}\\frac{15}{16}=1,\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nwhile the generation/register coordinate advances:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\delta_{\\rm loop}=1.\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\n","quote_sha256":"b00cb9f168244c03c4ffe97e8582aefd1bf138c8c4349faca8917b6901a8b36d"}]},{"id":"6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9","path":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/RELATED_LINEAGES/TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md","sha256":"1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065","source_status":"recovered TOL history/evaluation quotient; no named A/B maps invented","quotes":[{"char_start":13788,"char_end":14374,"line_start":698,"line_end":745,"quote":"## 14. Unevaluated versus evaluated harmonic spaces\n\nTo preserve operation order/history, the harmonic IR was split:\n\n\\[\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\mathcal H.\n\\]\n\nAn evaluation quotient:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nq_H=\\operatorname{eval}:\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\rightarrow\n\\mathcal H\n}\n\\]\n\npermits:\n\n\\[\nRL\\neq LR\n\\quad\\text{in }\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\]\n\nwhile:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\operatorname{eval}(RL)\n=\n\\operatorname{eval}(LR)\n=\n\\operatorname{eval}(O)\n=\n\\frac12\n}\n\\]\n\nin the evaluated harmonic space.\n\nThis is the harmonic-specific version of history-aware projected confluence.\n\n---\n\n","quote_sha256":"adf4e05246014f4515af33b9850a68e519f8ca776a82274ec395a8d11588c930"}]},{"id":"8ad7da0f6595b714fa87a52b5da6803200b6eee38cb09c7f81c6cf907624f756","path":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/SUN_DEEP_RECOVERY/SUN_Fludd_Kepler_Bridge_Registration_FREEZE_v0.1.md","sha256":"f1c0e211ca729997638b5b53b19159147f4f8b3d71be6dc28293e73897c7114d","source_status":"bridge-specific frozen hypothesis, including unresolved assembly/registration boundary","quotes":[{"char_start":244,"char_end":884,"line_start":6,"line_end":49,"quote":"## Frozen registration hypothesis\n\nLet\n\n\\[\nQ_{FK}=\n\\bigl(\n\\{\\mathrm{MI},\\mathrm{FA}\\},\n\\{e_{\\rm out},e_{\\rm return}\\}\n\\bigr)\n\\]\n\nwith\n\n\\[\ne_{\\rm out}:\\mathrm{MI}\\to\\mathrm{FA},\n\\qquad\ne_{\\rm return}:\\mathrm{FA}\\to\\mathrm{MI},\n\\qquad\ne_{\\rm return}\\neq \\bar e_{\\rm out}.\n\\]\n\nDefine the native Kepler loop\n\n\\[\n\\gamma_{FK}=e_{\\rm out}e_{\\rm return}.\n\\]\n\nThe single unresolved bridge-specific registration is frozen as\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\operatorname{Mon}([\\gamma_{FK}])=D\n}\n\\]\n\nwhere\n\n\\[\nD(p,k)=(p,k+1).\n\\]\n\nEquivalently: completion of the source-native Kepler MI→FA→MI return loop is hypothesized to carry the Fluddian octave/register transition.\n\n","quote_sha256":"406a5d7c0f652d82635c3c0e6700c8e0fb28e6aa89b1260ffc9e54f461f75fd0"},{"char_start":884,"char_end":3640,"line_start":50,"line_end":107,"quote":"## Evidence-status decomposition\n\n| Component | Status |\n|---|---|\n| \\(MI\\to FA\\to MI\\) ordered excursion | SOURCE-ATTESTED / NATIVE |\n| FA as the distinct intermediate pitch-class state | SOURCE-ATTESTED |\n| Exactly one modeled transient FA state | MINIMAL FAITHFUL REALIZATION, conditional on no unattested hidden states |\n| Distinct outbound and return channels | CONDITIONALLY DERIVED for nontrivial path-history/monodromy |\n| \\(e_{\\rm return}\\neq \\bar e_{\\rm out}\\) | MATHEMATICALLY REQUIRED for the chosen nontrivial-monodromy representation |\n| \\(\\rho=16/15\\) | DERIVED under frozen comma/enclosure constraints |\n| Total grade \\(+1\\) | CONDITIONALLY DERIVED from frozen \\(\\Phi\\), local cancellation, integer grade, and half-scale endpoint |\n| Boundary timing at \\(C_3\\) | CONDITIONALLY DERIVED from ten-visible capacity + ordinary sibling persistence |\n| Fludd typed lower/material/generative vs upper/formal/regenerative boundary | SOURCE-ATTESTED |\n| Fludd octave/register junction at that boundary | SOURCE-ATTESTED |\n| \\(\\operatorname{Mon}([\\gamma_{FK}])=D\\) | REMAINING ASSEMBLY / REGISTRATION HYPOTHESIS |\n| Full \\(B_{FK}\\) as universal SUN law | NOT ESTABLISHED |\n\n## What is no longer open\n\nThe project no longer treats the following as unexplained topology choices:\n\n1. why there is an MI→FA→MI return excursion;\n2. why FA is the native intermediate pitch-class state;\n3. why a nontrivial path-history model cannot collapse outward and return to one edge/inverse traversal;\n4. why the local scalar factor is \\(16/15\\) under the frozen enclosure;\n5. why the boundary must occur at \\(C_3\\), conditional on the ten-visible/persistence architecture.\n\n## Exact remaining claim\n\nThe first-edition evidence independently supplies:\n- exact comma correction;\n- returning MI→FA→MI motion;\n- typed Fludd boundary;\n- octave/register landing at that boundary.\n\nWhat it does **not** explicitly supply is the composition:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\text{Kepler returned MI}\n\\mapsto\n\\text{Fludd opposite octave/register sheet}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThat composition is the frozen bridge hypothesis.\n\n## Review / falsification trigger\n\nDo not reopen topology selection or numerical-constant search.\n\nReopen this freeze only if one of the following occurs:\n\n1. independent source/native evidence explicitly supports or contradicts the MI-return → Fludd-register assignment;\n2. an independently defined realization of the same native components yields a different register action while preserving all source-attested constraints;\n3. the two-channel monodromy model is shown to be mathematically inapplicable to the actual source-native state space.\n\nAbsent one of those triggers, the assembly remains a bridge-specific hypothesis and is not promoted into SUN's universal generative core.\n","quote_sha256":"d8e6ea12dc43d8968d8aeaa3141812b203d944d9d609321c39d685f7ac894193"}]}]},"source_checks":[{"source_id":"9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a53bead61e5d8b5a5e0315b259e8","sha256":"6a92f9710fa6cd2937b9b07c42315b7d9c80644bd453c659f17318f95c55f95d","quotes_checked":1},{"source_id":"32709e8763ac228cadc7cf5ef11c73eca6ada4257030855cc343ed4279474097","sha256":"66e5d2d763e55411993bfcf4ad07ca4cc0a708f624264e226abf51b90531e9dd","quotes_checked":1},{"source_id":"7d5a026c9df7d3fdf06382c966729a7cf3da22dbc4a1276c9f809f7a139ce965","sha256":"73b3171aa010c78121f2d7798011ce36f6e4891f4ef1409d25ed98aaca16fcfc","quotes_checked":1},{"source_id":"dd5004b2224cfaa99969f817c12d758ea41d503d4c93e8c680f681b001db7a77","sha256":"def5acfb2239f58fe91efbdab0096feba38a6d3e0a18a9ca20bf1e0e950dff94","quotes_checked":1},{"source_id":"6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9","sha256":"1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065","quotes_checked":1},{"source_id":"8ad7da0f6595b714fa87a52b5da6803200b6eee38cb09c7f81c6cf907624f756","sha256":"f1c0e211ca729997638b5b53b19159147f4f8b3d71be6dc28293e73897c7114d","quotes_checked":2}],"conventions":{"carrier":"Positive ideal pipe-length and frequency ratios; separate reciprocal actions.","units":"Ratios are dimensionless; a dimensional length or frequency requires its positive reference. No age-to-beat conversion.","frequency_normalization":"N(x)=x*2^k in[1,2); integer k retained. In the source Phi(a,m)=a*2^-m convention, m=-k.","word_composition":"Paths list operations in execution order; evaluated positive scalar multipliers commute, source path history does not disappear.","source_specific_FK_lift":"Phi and loop registration are retained bridge-specific hypotheses; not a newly established universal law."},"native_operations":{"SUN_length":{"R":{"numerator":2,"denominator":3,"exact":"2/3"},"L":{"numerator":3,"denominator":4,"exact":"3/4"},"O":{"numerator":1,"denominator":2,"exact":"1/2"},"inverses":{"R^-1":{"numerator":3,"denominator":2,"exact":"3/2"},"L^-1":{"numerator":4,"denominator":3,"exact":"4/3"},"O^-1":{"numerator":2,"denominator":1,"exact":"2"}}},"Chinese_length":{"D_L":{"numerator":2,"denominator":3,"exact":"2/3"},"U_L":{"numerator":4,"denominator":3,"exact":"4/3"},"ordered_D_then_U":[{"numerator":1,"denominator":1,"exact":"1"},{"operator":"D_L","numerator":2,"denominator":3,"exact":"2/3"},{"operator":"U_L","numerator":8,"denominator":9,"exact":"8/9"}]},"Chinese_frequency":{"D_f":{"numerator":3,"denominator":2,"exact":"3/2"},"U_f":{"numerator":3,"denominator":4,"exact":"3/4"},"ordered_D_then_U":[{"numerator":1,"denominator":1,"exact":"1"},{"operator":"D_f","numerator":3,"denominator":2,"exact":"3/2"},{"operator":"U_f","numerator":9,"denominator":8,"exact":"9/8"}]},"bridge_frequency":{"E_Earth":{"numerator":16,"denominator":15,"exact":"16/15"},"K_syntonic":{"numerator":81,"denominator":80,"exact":"81/80"}}},"connected_discriminator":{"target_E_over_K":{"numerator":256,"denominator":243,"exact":"256/243"},"reverse_five":{"exact":{"numerator":256,"denominator":243,"exact":"256/243"},"unreduced":{"numerator":32,"denominator":243,"exact":"32/243"},"normalization_k":3,"source_register_m":-3},"forward_seven":{"exact":{"numerator":2187,"denominator":2048,"exact":"2187/2048"},"unreduced":{"numerator":2187,"denominator":128,"exact":"2187/128"},"normalization_k":-4,"source_register_m":4},"shared_fifth_cycle_index_mod12":7,"forward_over_reverse_residual":{"numerator":531441,"denominator":524288,"exact":"531441/524288"},"old_bridge_on_forward7":{"numerator":177147,"denominator":163840,"exact":"177147/163840"},"required_bridge_on_forward7":{"numerator":32768,"denominator":32805,"exact":"32768/32805"},"required_bridge_over_old_bridge":{"numerator":524288,"denominator":531441,"exact":"524288/531441"},"residual_cents":23.460010384649014,"residual_cents_status":"binary64 descriptive value; exact ratio is authoritative; external Wolfram30digit result saved separately.","discriminating_observable":"Directed generation word together with register carries or a measured/source-specified residual. Mod12 address alone does not decide these exact realizations.","consequence":"Retaining the81/80 bridge and exact16/15 Earth target forces the reverse-five algebraic realization or an explicitly retained inverse-cycle correction on the forward-seven realization. The two words are not exact substitutes merely because their finite index matches.","not_claimed":"No unique global orientation; no claim that arbitrary inverse-generator words were the historical Chinese procedure."},"forward_semigroup_obstruction":{"exact_proof":"For nonnegative m,n and integer z, nu_3(D_f^m U_f^n 2^z)=m+n>=0, while nu_3(E/K)=-5. Thus no forward semigroup word plus octave shifts equals E/K.","group_solution":{"D_f_exponent":-2,"U_f_exponent":-3,"witness":{"numerator":256,"denominator":243,"exact":"256/243"}},"finite_sanity_bounds":{"m":[0,12],"n":[0,12],"z":[-20,20],"cases_checked":6929},"proof_scope":"Universal nonnegative-word obstruction follows from the exact valuation argument, not the finite sanity loop."},"history_observables":{"inverse_word_permutations":[{"word":["D_f^-1","D_f^-1","U_f^-1","U_f^-1","U_f^-1"],"path":[{"numerator":1,"denominator":1,"exact":"1"},{"operator":"D_f^-1","numerator":2,"denominator":3,"exact":"2/3"},{"operator":"D_f^-1","numerator":4,"denominator":9,"exact":"4/9"},{"operator":"U_f^-1","numerator":16,"denominator":27,"exact":"16/27"},{"operator":"U_f^-1","numerator":64,"denominator":81,"exact":"64/81"},{"operator":"U_f^-1","numerator":256,"denominator":243,"e