","status":"Computed and proved consequences; no empirical-success claim."},"outstanding":["Independent source-qualified phase observations","Whole musical/generational constraint integration beyond this source family","Class-growth/radius/rebound/fourth-axis laws","Prospective withheld-target testing after sufficient reconstruction"],"probe_designs":{"schema":"sunny.phase-probe-designs.v1","jevReceipt":"state/jev-receipts/000063-298ff24c136a.json","scope":"The recovered optional twelve-completion family with fixed coordinate labels and origin only; no historical phase observations are admitted.","priorArt":{"internal":"data/raw/recovered/f07f6e78ad08c09559939d044f382c5fb15a88ca56d10f2a6f5d060475e908fb/SUN_SOL_Orientation_Atlas.md","internalResult":"Section4.2 already gives all12 as one p-preserving orbit. Section3 distinguishes gauge changes from moving maps against fixed source labels.","external":"https://bdasgup.github.io/resume/publ/papers/ber3-swat04.pdf","reuse":"Reuse pair-separation/test-collection formulation. Exhaustively enumerate this small family; no approximation, arbitrary weighting, or claim of inventing test cover."},"counts":{"candidates":12,"wordOccurrences":144,"singleProbes":144,"unorderedDistinctProbePairs":10296,"minimalSufficientPairs":4608,"insufficientPairs":5688,"minimumProbes":2},"formula":"q(R^r L^l)=(r-l)b+l s mod6, b inZ6, s in{1,5}","criterion":"gcd(r1-l1,r2-l2,6)=1 AND (r1*l2-r2*l1) mod3 !=0","derivation":["For equal observations between candidates, write (r_i-l_i)Δb+l_iΔs=0 mod6 for i=1,2.","When Δs=0, only Δb=0 is allowed exactly when gcd(r1-l1,r2-l2,6)=1. Otherwise at least two different b values collide at fixed s.","When Δs=±2, work modulo2 and modulo3. Under the gcd condition at least one b coefficient is odd and one is nonzero modulo3.","Modulo2 forces Δb even. Modulo3 a nonzero Δs has a solution exactly when (r1-l1)l2-(r2-l2)l1=r1*l2-r2*l1 vanishes modulo3.","A nonzero determinant modulo3 forbids opposite-s collisions. If it vanishes, a modulo3 solution combines with the even modulo2 condition by CRT to produce a distinct colliding candidate.","Thus the two stated conditions are necessary and sufficient. No single phase observation has more than six values, so any sufficient pair is cardinality-minimal for twelve candidates."],"words":[{"id":"R0L0","r":0,"l":0,"angular":0,"phaseCoefficientB":0,"phaseCoefficientS":0,"expression":"R^0 L^0","sourceRefs":["9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a53bead61e5d8b5a5e0315b259e8","756f07b8874af89bc5f8ba247cb20b67e3d1b7da98eb35819bdd253247da75f2"]},{"id":"R0L1","r":0,"l":1,"angular":7,"phaseCoefficientB":5,"phaseCoefficientS":1,"expression":"R^0 L^1","sourceRefs":["9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a53bead61e5d8b5a5e0315b259e8","756f07b8874af89bc5f8ba247cb20b67e3d1b7da98eb35819bdd253247da75f2"]},{"id":"R0L2","r":0,"l":2,"angular":2,"phaseCoefficientB":4,"phaseCoefficientS":2,"expression":"R^0 L^2","sourceRefs":["9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a53bead61e5d8b5a5e0315b259e8","756f07b8874af89bc5f8ba247cb20b67e3d1b7da98eb35819bdd253247da75f2"]},{"id":"R0L3","r":0,"l":3,"angular":9,"phaseCoefficientB":3,"phaseCoefficientS":3,"expression":"R^0 L^3","sourceRefs":["9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a53bead61e5d8b5a5e0315b259e8","756f07b8874af89bc5f8ba247cb20b67e3d1b7da98eb35819bdd253247da75f2"]},{"id":"R0L4","r":0,"l":4,"angular":4,"phaseCoefficientB":2,"phaseCoefficientS":4,"expression":"R^0 L^4","sourceRefs":["9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a53bead61e5d8b5a5e0315b259e8","756f07b8874af89bc5f8ba247cb20b67e3d1b7da98eb35819bdd253247da75f2"]},{"id":"R0L5","r":0,"l":5,"angular":11,"phaseCoefficientB":1,"phaseCoefficientS":5,"expression":"R^0 L^5","sourceRefs":["9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a53bead61e5d8b5a5e0315b259e8","756f07b8874af89bc5f8ba247cb20b67e3d1b7da98eb35819bdd253247da75f2"]},{"id":"R0L6","r":0,"l":6,"angular":6,"phaseCoefficientB":0,"phaseCoefficientS":0,"expression":"R^0 L^6","sourceRefs":["9e03168cabf04e3887245d93c75f1f9d0034a5