ion":"3/2=R^{-1}; reverse traversal is explicit, not an unnoticed inversion of the descending SUN operator.","selection_limit":"These predicates distinguish transformations but do not elect a witness without independent source-defined boundary requirements."},{"id":"GT-JOINT-TIME-GEN","status":"new-source-derived-joint-invariant-executed","source_refs":["cainan_macro_transport","insertion_fifth_spiral"],"premises":["Shared Shelah-through-Terah main witness readings only.","Integer reported years and genealogical indices; common Arpachshad time origin and Adam-at-zero generation convention fixed across witnesses.","The retained fifth-traversal adapter is used only where explicitly stated."],"shift_lattice":{"basis_columns":[[50,130],[0,1]],"proof":"All MT→SP shifts are integer multiples of(50,0), and (50,0)=(650,0)-6(100,0) belongs to their integer span. The SP→Greek shift is(130,1). Thus the exact generated integer lattice H has the stated basis. Negative coefficients concern a representational lattice, not causal backwards generation.","smith_certificate":{"U":[[0,1],[-1,180]],"V":[[1,-1],[1,0]],"U_M_V":[[1,0],[0,50]],"determinant":50,"quotient":"Z²/H is isomorphic to Z50"}},"primitive_joint_character":"I(t,g)=t-130g mod50 = t+20g mod50","kernel_proof":"I(t,g)=0 iff t-130g=50k for some integerk, iff (t,g)=k(50,0)+g(130,1) lies inH. The map is ontoZ50 because I(1,0)=1. Therefore it exactly classifies the lattice cosets.","maximality_with_time_coefficient_one":"For t+b g modm to annihilate every actual shift, the zero-generation shifts force m to divide50 and the insertion forces b=-130 modm. The largest such positive integerm is50, with b=20.","actual_source_row_checks":[{"witness_transform":"MT_to_SP","descendant":"Shelah","delta_reported_years":100,"delta_genealogical_index":0,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"MT_to_SP","descendant":"Eber","delta_reported_years":200,"delta_genealogical_index":0,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"MT_to_SP","descendant":"Peleg","delta_reported_years":300,"delta_genealogical_index":0,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"MT_to_SP","descendant":"Reu","delta_reported_years":400,"delta_genealogical_index":0,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"MT_to_SP","descendant":"Serug","delta_reported_years":500,"delta_genealogical_index":0,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"MT_to_SP","descendant":"Nahor","delta_reported_years":600,"delta_genealogical_index":0,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"MT_to_SP","descendant":"Terah","delta_reported_years":650,"delta_genealogical_index":0,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"SP_to_Greek","descendant":"Shelah","delta_reported_years":130,"delta_genealogical_index":1,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"SP_to_Greek","descendant":"Eber","delta_reported_years":130,"delta_genealogical_index":1,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"SP_to_Greek","descendant":"Peleg","delta_reported_years":130,"delta_genealogical_index":1,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"SP_to_Greek","descendant":"Reu","delta_reported_years":130,"delta_genealogical_index":1,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"SP_to_Greek","descendant":"Serug","delta_reported_years":130,"delta_genealogical_index":1,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"SP_to_Greek","descendant":"Nahor","delta_reported_years":130,"delta_genealogical_index":1,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0},{"witness_transform":"SP_to_Greek","descendant":"Terah","delta_reported_years":130,"delta_genealogical_index":1,"delta_joint_phase_mod50":0}],"strict_refinement_of_pure_time":{"identity":"I mod10 = t mod10","counterexample_to_sufficiency_of_pure_time":{"states":[[0,0],[10,0]],"same_pure_time_mod10":0,"different_joint_mod50":[0,10]},"interpretation":"The joint invariant retains a factor of five beyond the common pure-time projection; this does not select a historical calendar or musical meter."},"not_constant_along_genealogical_dynamics":{"source_counterexample":"SP Eber→Peleg has delta(t,g)=(134,1), changingI by4 modulo50. With the retained origin, Shelah,Eber,Peleg haveI=25,25,29.","reason":"This is invariance across the specified witness representations, not a conservation law along every ancestral edge."},"conditional_music_address_consequence":{"premise":"Hold t modulo50 fixed, and use the declared fifth angular address p=7g modulo12.","derivation":"I depends on g modulo5, because20 has additive order5 modulo50. Pitch address depends on g modulo12. A generator shift preserving both must be divisible by5and12, hence60. The exact finite check finds60as the first positive return.","period":60,"boundary":"A representation-sufficiency result for these observables, not a new universal60generation class or a claim that time stays fixed during actual descent. Actual coupled insertion transports preserveI while changing time."},"gauge_limit":"Changing common time or generation origin shifts allI values by one common constant. Independent per-witness origin changes require an explicit gauge alignment before numericalI values are comparable.","falsifiers":["A new included zero-generation witness shift not divisible by50 changes the lattice index.","A source insertion vector other than(130,1) changes the joint coefficient or lattice.","A different declared generation convention, witness reading or origin requires recomputation.","A nonlinear year-to-performance adapter is outside this integer-year quotient."],"executed_adverse_controls":[{"altered_input":"Replace final MT→SP shift650 by651, keeping other listed shifts.","result":"The zero-generation time gcd becomes1, so the claimed Z50 quotient no longer survives."},{"altered_input":"Replace insertion(130,1) by(131,1).","result":"The original I changes by1 modulo50, so it fails the altered source vector; a recomputed coefficient would be required."}],"independent_solver":"docs/evidence/generational-joint-wolfram-check.json","historical_witness_elected":false},{"id":"GT-GEN-ADR","status":"reproduced-conditional-exclusion","source_refs":["generation_address_distinction","master_score"],"witness_values":[{"entity":"Ephraim","expanded_GEN":24,"shorter_GEN":23,"camp_ADR":7},{"entity":"Manasseh","expanded_GEN":24,"shorter_GEN":23,"camp_ADR":8},{"entity":"Benjamin","expanded_GEN":23,"shorter_GEN":22,"camp_ADR":9}],"proof":"A deterministic map of GEN alone must give Ephraim and Manasseh the same output. Fixed camp ADR gives7 and8, and the declared fifth traversal gives different pitch classes. Hence no GEN-only map can preserve both distinctions. Their shared institutional standing is not their biological depth.","excluded_joint_assumptions":["GEN alone fixes personal musical pitch/address","Distinct fixed Numbers2 tribal addresses must remain distinct under the declared address/pitch adapter"],"named_identity_branches":{"Benjamin_Ephraim":"Two distinct tribal positions cannot be one local W72 binary fiber if tribe fixes p; no rejection of the tradition itself.","Zebulun_siblings":"Same tribal p is compatible in principle; tau/beta assignment is still not supplied.","Levite_Amram":"Outside ordinary outer-camp carrier unless a separate registered map is supplied."},"temporal_limit":"Eldad/Medad activities and quail-related contribution have source event order but no corresponding numerical birth/duration data. Do not transfer the Cainan5year offsets or treat prophecy presentation order as three measured beats."},{"id":"GT-720-REGISTER","status":"new-conditional-compatibility-constraint","source_refs":["two_turn_class_hunch","sophia_boundary_aliases","master_score"],"premises":["User-proposed two360degree turns per class lift retained with its original exploratory qualification.","For this compatibility test only: same angular wheel for retained R5/L7 steps,30degrees per address step; one RL circuit is360degrees.","SUN RL=O halves the scalar center and increments descent-positive acoustic grade by1."],"proof":"After k RL circuits, angle=360k and acoustic grade increment=k. A720degree class counter h=floor(k/2) leaves parity epsilon=k mod2. Thus acoustic grade increment=2h+epsilon. At720degrees h=1 but acoustic grade increment=2 and C_new/C_old=1/4.","consequence":"A720degree class lift cannot silently be identified with a single acoustic O-halving under the shared-angle premises. Keep class and register separate, or supply a different explicit bridge/angle convention.","minimal_state_requirement":"If a rule distinguishes alternating whole-turn returns, phase modulo360 alone is insufficient; preserve at least return parity or integer winding. This does not identify parity with W72 beta.","execution":[{"RL_circuits":0,"angle_degrees_if_common_angle":0,"720_class_counter":0,"circuit_parity_separate_unidentified_coordinate":0,"acoustic_register_increment":0,"SUN_scalar_ratio":"1"},{"RL_circuits":1,"angle_degrees_if_common_angle":360,"720_class_counter":0,"circuit_parity_separate_unidentified_coordinate":1,"acoustic_register_increment":1,"SUN_scalar_ratio":"1/2"},{"RL_circuits":2,"angle_degrees_if_common_angle":720,"720_class_counter":1,"circuit_parity_separate_unidentified_coordinate":0,"acoustic_register_increment":2,"SUN_scalar_ratio":"1/4"},{"RL_circuits":3,"angle_degrees_if_common_angle":1080,"720_class_counter":1,"circuit_parity_separate_unidentified_coordinate":1,"acoustic_register_increment":3,"SUN_scalar_ratio":"1/8"},{"RL_circuits":4,"angle_degrees_if_common_angle":1440,"720_class_counter":2,"circuit_parity_separate_unidentified_coordinate":0,"acoustic_register_increment":4,"SUN_scalar_ratio":"1/16"},{"RL_circuits":5,"angle_degrees_if_common_angle":1800,"720_class_counter":2,"circuit_parity_separate_unidentified_coordinate":1,"acoustic_register_increment":5,"SUN_scalar_ratio":"1/32"},{"RL_circuits":6,"angle_degrees_if_common_angle":2160,"720_class_counter":3,"circuit_parity_separate_unidentified_coordinate":0,"acoustic_register_inc