y inheritance model are equivalent."},"queryRegister":[{"id":"HD-Q1","need":"Context-matched independently licensed donor negative state plus recipient positive state, with their relative date bounds.","consequence":"Can exclude the specified donor-to-recipient edge if the donor onset lower bound is later than the recipient acquisition upper bound.","missing":"Both phonetic licenses, exact witness contexts and independently justified bounds; an absent transcription is not a negative phone observation."},{"id":"HD-Q2","need":"Independently bounded period when this transmission could occur, plus recipient acquisition upper bound.","consequence":"Can exclude this proposed contact if its earliest possible date follows recipient acquisition.","missing":"Contact opportunity bounds cannot be inferred merely from failing to find a contact record; third-party and other episodes remain separate."},{"id":"HD-Q3","need":"Independently justified transcription-to-phone mapping in the exact source context.","consequence":"Can separate a pure written-normalization explanation from a changed-pronunciation explanation.","missing":"Received vowel letters and current scholarly reconstructed phones are not independent ancient acoustic observations; hybrid explanations survive."},{"id":"HD-Q4","need":"Evidence constraining transmission, copying or lineage independently of the sound-state trajectories.","consequence":"Required to distinguish contact from an observationally identical independent-change realization when their full trajectories coincide.","missing":"More sound-state samples, even perfect all-time phone trajectories in the counterexample, do not identify the causal edge."}],"priorArt":{"standingProtocol":"G16: recurring original-source prior art, P0-A baseline, controlled First &3/4 Order exposure and exact transfer/reuse conditions.","inheritedBaseline":"state/research/reactivation/symbols/p0a-14-baseline.json","currentCensusStatus":"Bounded mainstream method extension; complete updated14question census and ten-question/M1-M12 heterodox phase remain open. No exhaustive novelty claim.","sources":[{"id":"erdem-2005","title":"Temporal Phylogenetic Networks and Logic Programming","authors":"Esra Erdem; Vladimir Lifschitz; Don Ringe","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cs/0508129","path":"state/delivery-2026-11-07/history-discriminator/primary/erdem-2005.pdf","sha256":"b34aee06b3485aa231e1f14474f571f41aca66bb9600113c897340130a1ce7a7","bytes":263006,"status":"preserved-existing","httpStatus":null,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-07T22:23:39.644584+00:00","scope":"Primary-method paper bytes, not evidence of a Hebrew historical event"},{"id":"angluin-1988","title":"Queries and Concept Learning","authors":"Dana Angluin","url":"https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~lreyzin/papers/angluin88.pdf","path":"state/delivery-2026-11-07/history-discriminator/primary/angluin-1988.pdf","sha256":"2662d43f8a34689886a3e2f2b266e5c0f1059a66b30759a3c8366a6f37d2dd8c","bytes":1445221,"status":"preserved-existing","httpStatus":null,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-07T22:23:39.645839+00:00","scope":"Primary-method paper bytes, not evidence of a Hebrew historical event"},{"id":"dechter-1991","title":"Temporal constraint networks","authors":"Rina Dechter; Itay Meiri; Judea Pearl","url":"https://ftp.cs.ucla.edu/pub/stat_ser/r113-L-reprint.pdf","path":"state/delivery-2026-11-07/history-discriminator/primary/dechter-1991.pdf","sha256":"b89a1f705a89be8a1bc140f90ad0d3eadba5c1507da7475521df05effc24f732","bytes":3061457,"status":"retrieved","httpStatus":200,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-07T22:23:41.579080+00:00","scope":"Primary-method paper bytes, not evidence of a Hebrew historical event"}],"inspected":[{"id":"erdem-2005","pages":[1,2,3],"reuse":"Model transmission separately from tree ancestry; contact requires contemporary communities.","limit":"The paper models linguistic networks, not sacred original phonetics or a musical geometry."},{"id":"angluin-1988","pages":[1,2,3],"reuse":"Specify allowed observation 